  "claim": "Joan Baez's hit recording from Quad Studios Nashville originally featured lead vocals from Levon Helm of The Band.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Quad Studios Nashville. Sentence: The studio immediately became the home of many major recording sessions including Neil Young's \"Harvest\" album which included the single \"Heart of Gold,\" Jimmy Buffett's biggest hit \"Margaritaville\" from his best selling album Changes In Latitudes, Changes In Attitudes, much of Joan Baez' early 1970s work, including her hit recording of \"The Night They Drove Old Dixie Down\" and Dobie Gray's R&B classic \"Drift Away.\"\nPage: The Night They Drove Old Dixie Down. Sentence: Levon Helm provided the lead vocals.",
