        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "c60b68bd-b508-5208-bc27-05fc9fbd33c2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Quad Studios Nashville\n- People: Neil Young, Jimmy Buffett, Joan Baez, Dobie Gray, Levon Helm\n- Products: Harvest, Heart of Gold, Margaritaville, Changes In Latitudes, Changes In Attitudes, The Night They Drove Old Dixie Down, Drift Away\n- Topics: major recording sessions, lead vocals\n\nFacts:\n- Quad Studios Nashville immediately became the site of major recording sessions for Neil Young's album \"Harvest,\" which included the single \"Heart of Gold.\"\n- Quad Studios Nashville hosted major recording sessions for Jimmy Buffett's hit \"Margaritaville\" from his best-selling album \"Changes In Latitudes, Changes In Attitudes.\"\n- Quad Studios Nashville hosted much of Joan Baez's early 1970s work, including her hit recording of \"The Night They Drove Old Dixie Down.\"\n- Levon Helm provided the lead vocals on \"The Night They Drove Old Dixie Down.\"\n- Quad Studios Nashville hosted major recording sessions for Dobie Gray's R&B song \"Drift Away.\"",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "5ba04ff0-d3b2-5b9e-a551-5080a6a2f10f",
        "text": "Page: Quad Studios Nashville. Sentence: The studio immediately became the home of many major recording sessions including Neil Young's \"Harvest\" album which included the single \"Heart of Gold,\" Jimmy Buffett's biggest hit \"Margaritaville\" from his best selling album Changes In Latitudes, Changes In Attitudes, much of Joan Baez' early 1970s work, including her hit recording of \"The Night They Drove Old Dixie Down\" and Dobie Gray's R&B classic \"Drift Away.\"\nPage: The Night They Drove Old Dixie Down. Sentence: Levon Helm provided the lead vocals.",
